{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01154",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 6.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Let me think, hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.53,
      "end_seconds": 11.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.75,
      "end_seconds": 17.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Um, so... constipation. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.53,
      "end_seconds": 22.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.41,
      "end_seconds": 29.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "It's been four weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.26,
      "end_seconds": 34.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.45,
      "end_seconds": 40.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I'd give it a eight, uh, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.24,
      "end_seconds": 44.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.17,
      "end_seconds": 59.73,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "Hmm, it usually comes with a heavy feeling in the lower tummy. The heavy feeling in the lower tummy? That's been for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.07,
      "end_seconds": 76.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Right, any fever, weight loss or pain on passing stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.29,
      "end_seconds": 79.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.54,
      "end_seconds": 84.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Did you get black stools or abdominal swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.8,
      "end_seconds": 90.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Yeah, no, no black stools or abdominal swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.58,
      "end_seconds": 95.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.14,
      "end_seconds": 100.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.58,
      "end_seconds": 103.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.2,
      "end_seconds": 106.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Oh, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.08,
      "end_seconds": 114.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "So, do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.13,
      "end_seconds": 120.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid. I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.47,
      "end_seconds": 132.68,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Yes, diabetes is known to us, good to have that clear. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.65,
      "end_seconds": 145.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.84,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.25,
      "end_seconds": 163.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Alright, have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.71,
      "end_seconds": 168.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Just a varicose vein procedure, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.19,
      "end_seconds": 172.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.73,
      "end_seconds": 178.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "I mean, you know, it's Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.16,
      "end_seconds": 181.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "How long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.64,
      "end_seconds": 193.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "About about a month. Ah, it's glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. Cremaffin, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.98,
      "end_seconds": 197.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "How long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.47,
      "end_seconds": 206.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "For about a month. Right, uh, I was on metformin before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.57,
      "end_seconds": 212.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.89,
      "end_seconds": 218.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Okay, so my mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.17,
      "end_seconds": 238.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.69,
      "end_seconds": 243.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Yeah, no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.74,
      "end_seconds": 247.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.47,
      "end_seconds": 256.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.79,
      "end_seconds": 277.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.8, BP is 125 over 82, pulse 83, saturation 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.17,
      "end_seconds": 283.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.59,
      "end_seconds": 286.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.16,
      "end_seconds": 308.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "I can feel firm stool in the left lower abdomen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.41,
      "end_seconds": 312.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.83,
      "end_seconds": 328.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "There's no mass in the tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.27,
      "end_seconds": 342.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. From what you've told me and what I found, it points towards chronic constipation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.35,
      "end_seconds": 349.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Oh, what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.33,
      "end_seconds": 365.88,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like chronic constipation, but I'd like to confirm. I'm going to order blood tests, for constipation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 367.46,
      "end_seconds": 370.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "The earliest is Tuesday, 9 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.94,
      "end_seconds": 392.03,
      "duration_seconds": 21.09,
      "text": "For this, lactulose, 15 ml, at night, for two weeks. You take it by mouth. It's for constipation. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. More fibre, more water, and give yourself ten unhurried minutes after breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.62,
      "end_seconds": 401.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Let's review you in three weeks. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.91,
      "end_seconds": 413.52,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "So, I take the lactulose, 15 ml, at night and come back in three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.3,
      "end_seconds": 419.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.78,
      "end_seconds": 428.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.29,
      "end_seconds": 431.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}